{"name":"King Tide","hex":"#2a7279","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"king tide","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An unusually high spring tide that occurs during full moon in the summer and winter months (when the earth is at perihelion and the earth, moon and sun are aligned)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/king_tide"}],"entries":[{"title":"King tide","blocks":[{"text":"A king tide is an especially high spring tide, especially the perigean spring tides which occur three or four times a year. King tide is not a scientific term, nor is it used in a scientific context."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/CSIRO_ScienceImage_10726_The_effects_of_a_king_tide_on_Queenslands_Gold_Coast.jpg/330px-CSIRO_ScienceImage_10726_The_effects_of_a_king_tide_on_Queenslands_Gold_Coast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_tide","wikidata":"Q1303867"},{"title":"King Tide (album)","blocks":[{"text":"King Tide is the fifth studio album released by Australian rock band Weddings Parties Anything. The album was released in October 1993 on the RooArt label and peaked at No. 20 on the ARIA Album Charts."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d7/Wpa-kingtide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Tide_(album)","wikidata":"Q6412107"},{"title":"King","blocks":[{"text":"King is a royal title given to a male monarch. A king is an absolute monarch if he holds unrestricted governmental power or exercises full sovereignty over a nation. In a modern context, the title may refer to the ruler of one of a number of modern monarchies. The title of king is used alongside other titles for monarchs: in the West, emperor, grand prince, prince, archduke, duke or grand duke, and in the Islamic world, malik, sultan, emir or hakim, among others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg/330px-Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King","wikidata":"Q12097"},{"title":"Tide","blocks":[{"text":"Tides are the periodic rise and fall of sea level resulting from the differential gravitational forces exerted primarily by the Moon and the Sun, combined with inertial effects associated with the Earth–Moon system’s orbital motion and the Earth's rotation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Tide_overview.svg/330px-Tide_overview.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tide","wikidata":"Q23384"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/King_Charles_III_%28July_2023%29.jpg/500px-King_Charles_III_%28July_2023%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/King_Charles_III_%28July_2023%29.jpg/500px-King_Charles_III_%28July_2023%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKing_Charles_III_(July_2023).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Bilateral_Meeting_with_King_Hamad_bin_Isa_Al_Khalifa_-_54551307222_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Bilateral_Meeting_with_King_Hamad_bin_Isa_Al_Khalifa_-_54551307222_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Bilateral_Meeting_with_King_Hamad_bin_Isa_Al_Khalifa_-_54551307222_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Bilateral_Meeting_with_King_Hamad_bin_Isa_Al_Khalifa_-_54551307222_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/